Bundled fonts
-------------

The dashboard ships its typefaces as woff2 files inside the package and loads
them from disk. It requests no font, stylesheet or script from a third party at
runtime, so the dashboard works with no network at all - and does not tell
anyone else when you open it.

Each of these is licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, which permits
bundling and commercial use and requires that this notice travel with the fonts.
The full text of each licence is in LICENSES/.

  Bricolage Grotesque  Copyright 2022 The Bricolage Grotesque Project Authors
                       https://github.com/ateliertriay/bricolage
  Geist                Copyright 2024 The Geist Project Authors
                       https://github.com/vercel/geist-font
  Geist Mono           Copyright 2024 The Geist Project Authors
                       https://github.com/vercel/geist-font
  Plus Jakarta Sans    Copyright 2020 The Plus Jakarta Sans Project Authors
                       https://github.com/tokotype/PlusJakartaSans
  Space Grotesk        Copyright 2020 The Space Grotesk Project Authors
                       https://github.com/floriankarsten/space-grotesk

None of the fonts has been modified, so no Reserved Font Name applies.

Bundled browser code
--------------------

The dashboard also ships as a pre-built bundle, and that bundle inlines its
third-party libraries - React, CodeMirror, xterm.js, highlight.js, visx,
Tailwind and their dependencies. The package carries no node_modules, so unlike
the CLI's dependencies these licences do not arrive with the code, and
minification strips the copyright comments the sources carry.

Every one of them is reproduced in full, with its version and copyright line,
in LICENSES/third-party-browser.txt. That file is generated from the build's
own sourcemaps, so it lists the code that is actually in the bundle rather than
what the manifest implies. The licences are MIT, ISC, BSD-3-Clause and OFL-1.1.

The CLI is a separate case: its dependencies stay external and are installed
from npm with their own licence files intact.
